  "generated_text": "First, identify the elements of the set \\( S \\):\n\\[ S = \\{2^0, 2^1, 2^2, \\ldots, 2^{10}\\} \\]\n\\[ S = \\{1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256, 512\\} \\]\n\nNext, consider all possible positive differences of pairs of elements in \\( S \\). Notice that each difference is a power of 2:\n\\[ 2 - 1 = 1 \\]\n\\[ 4 - 2 = 2 \\]\n\\[ 8 - 4 = 4 \\]\n\\[ 16 - 8 = 8 \\]\n\\[ 32 - 16 = 16 \\]\n\\[ 64 - 32 = 32 \\]\n\nNow, sum these differences:\n\\[ 1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 + 32 = 63 \\]\n\nThus, the sum \\( N \\) of all possible positive differences is:\n\\boxed{63}",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[63, '63']",
    "gold_answer": "When computing $N$, the number $2^x$ will be added $x$ times (for terms $2^x-2^0$, $2^x-2^1$, $\\dots,$ $2^x - 2^{x-1}$), and subtracted $10-x$ times. Hence, $N$ can be computed as $$N=10\\cdot 2^{10} + 8\\cdot 2^9 + 6\\cdot 2^8 + \\cdots - 8\\cdot 2^1 - 10\\cdot 2^0.$$Then\n\\begin{align*}\nN & = 10(2^{10}-1) + 8(2^9 - 2^1) + 6(2^8-2^2) + 4(2^7-2^3) + 2(2^6-2^4) \\\\\n& = 10(1023) + 8(510) + 6(252) + 4(120) + 2(48) \\\\\n& = 10(1000+23) + 8(500+10) + 6(250+2) + 480 + 96 \\\\\n&= \\boxed{16398}.\n\\end{align*}",
    "is_correct": false
  },
